# Local-only working doc — kept on disk, not committed
PROMPT-standardize-parts-A-D.md

# The demo-authoring template. Lives in Google Drive; a working copy sits here
# while it is being revised, and is carried back out by hand. Deliberately NOT
# tracked — the catalog is not its home, and committing it would create a second
# source of truth to drift against the Drive original.
# The in-repo standard that IS tracked is audits/_MASTER-TEMPLATE.md.
CRYPTO-LAB-TEMPLATE*.md

# Installed by tools/package.json for the verification renderers.
tools/node_modules/

# Read-only exports of each lab's remote default branch, written by
# tools/depth-audit.js. Disposable: re-created from GitHub on demand, and never
# a source of truth — the remote is.
.scratch/

# Parked work-in-progress: a majors-only dependency pass, held out of commits on
# purpose and carrying a known indentation bug. Ignored rather than left merely
# untracked, because untracked is exactly the state a broad `git add` sweeps up —
# this file rode into a commit twice, on 2026-09-22 and again on 2026-09-29, both
# times byte-identical. The precedent is f3afc10 (2026-08-04), which prescribed
# this for the demo-authoring template and was not applied here at the time.
tools/majors-sync.js
chat.md

# Playwright output from the browser suites, which write screenshots here by
# explicit path (tests/council-vault-browser.test.cjs and its siblings create
# test-results/<game>/ and save PNGs into it). Disposable: re-created by the
# next run, and never a source of truth — the assertions are.
#
# Ignored rather than left merely untracked, for the reason the entry above
# records: untracked is exactly the state a broad `git add` sweeps up. Running
# the suites leaves a `?? test-results/` in `git status`, so this would have
# ridden into a commit as a directory of binary screenshots the first time
# anyone staged a directory instead of a path.
test-results/

# A GitHub PAT parked in the repo root. Gitignored so a broad `git add` cannot
# sweep it in — CLAUDE.md records a 573-line parked file swept twice, a week
# apart, byte for byte, because the remedy was "untrack it" rather than "ignore it".
pat
pat.*
*.pat
